===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
[[File:Värmland sheep white ram.jpg|thumb|This sheep has '''horns'''.]]
[[File:Garde Républicaine en concert dans les jardins de l'Hotel du Minsitre des Affaires Etrangères (Quai d'Orsay) (5).jpg|thumb|A man playing a '''horn'''.]]

# {{senseid|en|Q82025}}{{lb|en|countable|zootomy}} A hard [[growth]] of [[keratin]] that protrudes from the top of the [[head]] of certain [[animal]]s, usually [[paired]].
# Any similar real or imaginary growth or [[projection]] such as the elongated [[tusk]] of a [[narwhal]], the [[eyestalk]] of a [[snail]], the pointed growth on the nose of a [[rhinoceros]], or the hornlike projection on the head of a [[demon]] or similar.
# {{senseid|en|Q834007}} An [[antler]].
# {{senseid|en|Q29838373}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} The hard substance from which animals' horns are made, sometimes used by man as a material for making various objects.
#: {{syn|en|keratin}}
#: {{ux|en|an umbrella with a handle made of '''horn'''}}
# A vessel made from a horn, to contain [[drink]], [[ink]], [[gunpowder]], etc.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1775|author={{w|William Mason (poet)|William Mason}}|title=The Poems of Mr. Gray. To which are prefixed Memoirs of his Life and Writings by W. Mason.|passage='''horns''' of mead and ale}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1828|author=Thomas Keightley|authorlink=Thomas Keightley|title=The Fairy Mythology|volume=I|location=London|publisher=William Harrison Ainsworth|page=179|passage=The one brought out a filled up '''horn'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Neil Gaiman|authorlink=Neil Gaiman|publisher=Bloomsbury Publishing|title=Norse Mythology|page=143|passage=I guarantee you a mighty feast, '''horns''' of ale, and afterwards wrestling and racing and contests of strength.}}
# An [[object]] whose shape resembles a horn, such as [[cornucopia]] or the point of an [[anvil]].
## One of the two [[corner]]s of a [[crescent]], particularly of the crescent [[moon]]
##* {{RQ:Thomson Winter|year=1768|page=169|lines=123–125|passage=[W]hile riſing ſlow, / Blank, in the leaden-colour'd eaſt, the moon / Wears a wan circle round her blunted '''horns'''.}}
## The high pommel of a saddle; also, either of the projections on a lady's saddle for supporting the leg.
##* {{quote-book|en |author={{w|Dorothy M. Johnson}}|year=1950|newversion=in |type2=book |editor2=|title=Prairie Kid|title2=Indian Country|location2=London |publisher2=Corgi|year2=1961 |page2=51|text=Buck Saddler carried a rifle and a shotgun on the saddle, and two belts of cartridges slung over the '''horn'''.}}
## {{senseid|en|Q218626}} {{lb|en|architectural element}} The [[Ionic]] [[volute]].
## {{lb|en|nautical}} The outer end of a [[crosstree]]; also, one of the projections forming the jaws of a [[gaff]], [[boom]], etc.
## {{lb|en|carpentry}} A curved projection on the fore part of a [[plane]].
## One of the projections at the four corners of the [[Jewish]] [[altar]] of burnt offering.
##* {{RQ:KJV|1 Kings|2|28|passage=Joab {{...}} caught hold on the '''horns''' of the altar}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any of several [[musical]] [[wind instrument]]s.
# {{senseid|en|Q2996954}} {{lb|en|countable|musical instrument}} An instrument resembling a musical horn and used to signal others.
#: {{ux|en|hunting '''horn'''}}
# {{lb|en|countable|automotive}} A loud [[alarm]], especially one on a motor vehicle.
#: {{syn|en|hooter|klaxon}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|sports}} A sound signaling the expiration of time.
#: {{ux|en|The shot was after the '''horn''' and therefore did not count.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[conical]] device used to direct [[wave]]s.
#: {{syn|en|funnel}}
#: {{ux|en|antenna '''horn'''}}
#: {{ux|en|loudspeaker '''horn'''}}
# {{senseid|en|Q180744}} {{lb|en|informal|musical instrument|countable}} Generally, any [[brass]] wind instrument.
# {{senseid|en|Q11035}} {{lb|en|slang|countable}} A [[telephone]].
#: {{syn|en|[[blower]] {{q|UK}}|[[dog and bone]] {{q|Cockney rhyming slang}}|phone}}
#: {{ux|en|Get him [[on the horn|on the '''horn''']] so that we can have a discussion about this.}}
# {{senseid|en|erection}} {{lb|en|vulgar|slang|with definite article}} An [[erection]] of the penis.
#: {{syn|en|[[boner]] {{q|US}}|hard-on|stiffy}}
# {{senseid|en|Q34763}} {{lb|en|countable|geography}} A [[peninsula]] or [[project]]ing tract of land.
#: {{syn|en|peninsula}}
#: {{ux|en|to navigate around the '''horn'''}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1902|author=John Buchan|title=The Outgoing of the Tide
|passage=But nowhere are there queerer waters than in our own parish of Caulds, at the place called the Sker Bay, where between two '''horns''' of land a shallow estuary receives the stream of the Sker.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q1628306}} {{lb|en|countable}} A [[diacritical mark]] that may be attached to the top right corner of the letters '''o''' and '''u''' when writing in [[Vietnamese]], thus forming '''ơ''' and '''ư'''.
# {{lb|en|botany}} An incurved, tapering and pointed appendage found in the flowers of the [[milkweed]] ({{taxfmt|Asclepias|genus}}).
# {{lb|en|military}} In naval mine warfare, a projection from the [[mine]] [[shell]] of some contact mines which, when broken or bent by contact, causes the mine to fire.

====Usage notes====
* When used alone to refer to an instrument, {{m|en|horn}} can mean either {{m|en|hunting horn}} or {{m|en|French horn}}, depending on context. Other instruments are identified by specific adjectives such as {{m|en|English horn}} or {{m|en|basset horn}}.

