# {{senseid|en|identicalness}} {{lb|en|now chiefly in technical usage}} [[sameness|Sameness]], [[identicalness]]; the quality or fact of (several specified things) being the same.
#: {{syn|en|identicalness|identicality|sameness|Thesaurus:sameness}}
#: {{ant|en|unidenticality|nonidentity|Thesaurus:difference}}
#: {{cot|en|equivalence|;|fungibility|interchangeability|;|commensurateness|;|similarity|;|resemblance}}
#: {{ux|en|Benjamin Franklin established the '''identity''' of electricity and lightning.}}
#* {{RQ:More Iniquity|part=2|chapter=X|page=264|passage=But whenas a leſſer number of Agreements in each Paralleliſm (provided there were nothing contrary) could not but have been a ſtrong preſumption of the '''Identity''' of the Subjects of the Viſions in each Chapter, I mean, ''That the Two-horned Beaſt and the Whore are one, and the Seven-headed Beaſt in each Chapter the ſame''; how fully aſſured muſt we needs be of theſe '''Identities''', the Agreements of theſe two Paralleliſms (thoſe paſſages onely excepted of which I have given ſo fair an account) perfectly exhauſting the whole ſubſtance of each Chapter?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1997|title=Hydrothermal Vent Fauna|journal=Advances in Marine Biology: The Biogeography of the Oceans|page=111|text={{...}} suggesting the two are different stages of the same species. The '''identity''' of the two species is further suggested by allozyme analysis {{...}}}}
# {{senseid|en|selfhood}} The [[difference]] or [[character]] that marks off an [[individual]] or [[collective]] from the [[rest]] of the same kind; [[selfhood]]; the sense of who something or someone or oneself is, or the [[recurring]] [[characteristic]]s that [[enable]] the [[recognition]] of such an [[individual]] or [[group]] by others or themselves.
#: {{syn|en|individuality|Thesaurus:selfhood}}
#: {{ux|en|I've been through so many changes, I have no sense of '''identity'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|This nation has a strong '''identity'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Joyce Dubliners|page=277|passage=His own '''identity''' was fading out into a grey impalpable world: the solid world itself which these dead had one time reared and lived in was dissolving and dwindling.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=28 July 2021|author={{w|Fausto Cercignani}}|title=On the alleged existence of a vowel {{IPAchar|/yː/}} in early Modern English|doi=10.1017/S1360674321000083|journal={{w|English Language and Linguistics}}|volume=26|issue=2|publisher={{w|Cambridge University Press}}|page=2|passage=On the other hand, ME {{IPAchar|/ɛu/}} preserved its '''identity''' into the early Modern English period, and the early writers on orthography and pronunciation normally distinguish between lME {{IPAchar|/iu/}} and lME {{IPAchar|/ɛu/}}, the latter of which occurs in words with eME {{IPAchar|/ɛː/}} like {{l|en|dew}} (OE {{l|ang|dēaw}}), {{l|en|few}} (OE {{l|ang|feaw|fēawe}}), {{l|en|hew}} (OE {{l|ang|hēawan}}), {{l|en|sew}} (eME ē < ĕ, OE {{l|ang|seowian}}), shrew (OE {{l|ang|scrēawa}}), etc.}}
# {{senseid|en|persona or identifier}} A [[name]] or [[persona]]—a mask or appearance one presents to the world—by which one is known.
#: {{ux|en|This criminal has taken on several '''identities'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|In this show, the competitor's '''identity''' will remain secret until after the vote.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} An [[equation]] which always holds true regardless of the choice of input [[variable]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The equation (''x''+''y'')(''x''−''y'') {{=}} ''x''<sup>2</sup>−''y''<sup>2</sup> is an algebraic '''identity.''' It is true regardless of the values of ''x'' and ''y''.}}
# {{senseid|en|identity function, in mathematics}} {{lb|en|algebra|computing}} Any [[function]] which [[map]]s all elements of its [[domain]] to themselves.
#: {{syn|en|identity function}}
# {{lb|en|algebra}} An element of an algebraic structure which, when applied to another element under an operation in that structure, yields this second element.
#: {{ux|en|Zero is the '''identity''' for the addition of real numbers.}}
# {{senseid|en|a well-known or famous person}} {{lb|en|Australia|NZ}} A [[well-known]] or [[famous]] person.
#: {{syn|en|celebrity|personality}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1887 July 19|title=Drowned at Williamstown|url=http://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/190634718|journal=The Age|location=Melbourne|text=The body of a well known old '''identity''' named James Conroy […] was found in the water yesterday afternoon…}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 4 2013|title=Cricket '''identities''' consult lawyers|journal=New Zealand Herald|titleurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130410135936/http://www.nzherald.co.nz/sport/news/article.cfm?c_id=4&objectid=10875363}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=January 13 2016|title=Kings Cross '''identities''' arrested in connection with murder|journal=The Sydney Morning Herald|titleurl=http://www.smh.com.au/nsw/kings-cross-identities-arrested-in-connection-with-murder-20160113-gm4s1g.html|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20161016093648/http://www.smh.com.au:80/nsw/kings-cross-identities-arrested-in-connection-with-murder-20160113-gm4s1g.html|archivedate=16 October 2016}}
