====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# To [[want]] (something) to [[happen]], with a sense of [[expectation]] that it [[might]] {{+obj|en|:that(clause)|clause<q:informal>|:so/:not<q:negative>}}.
#: {{ux|en|They are '''hoping''' it does not rain, but I expect it will.}}
#: {{ux|en|He's still '''hoping''' that everything will [[turn out]] fine.}}
#: {{ux|en|&mdash; Is he [[going to]] [[shut up]] soon? &mdash; I '''hope''' so.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm [[going to]] get a new car. I '''hope''' it will be better than the last one.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'd '''hope'''d I'd find a job, but I never did, so I was '''hoping''' you could lend me some cash.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''hope''' {to - (that) I'll} have finished by next Sat [[at the latest]].}}
#* {{RQ:Poe Tamerlane|chapter=Tamerlane|passage=I would not call thee fool, old man. / But hope is not a gift of thine; / If I ''can'' '''hope''' (O God! I can) / It falls from an eternal shrine.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=October|title=The winter timetables of British Railways: Southern Region|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=593|text=It is to be '''hoped''' that some corresponding smartening up of these other schedules may be expected before long.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-08|volume=407|issue=8839|page=55|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/business/21579011-president-proposes-new-round-intellectual-property-reform-obama-goes-troll-hunting Obama goes troll-hunting]
|passage=The solitary, lumbering trolls of Scandinavian mythology would sometimes be turned to stone by exposure to sunlight. Barack Obama is '''hoping''' that several measures announced on June 4th will have a similarly paralysing effect on their modern incarnation, the patent troll.}}
# {{lb|en|catenative}} To [[intend]] to do something and [[look forward]] to the prospect of having done it {{+obj|en|:to(inf)}}.
#: {{ux|en|I '''hope''' to succeed.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''hope''' to be [[going back]] again soon.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was '''hoping''' to find a pair of jeans, but I couldn't.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=10|passage=He looked round the poor room, at the distempered walls, and the bad engravings in meretricious frames, the crinkly paper and wax flowers on the chiffonier; and he thought of a room like Father Bryan's, with panelling, with cut glass, with tulips in silver pots, such a room as he had '''hoped''' to have for his own.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[expect]] [[optimistically]] that one might [[get]] something {{q|either a change in circumstance or an object}} {{+obj|en|:for}}.
#: {{ux|en|They're '''hoping''' for the best, but I don't think it's looking very good.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm '''hoping''' for my boss to offer me a [[pay raise]].}}
#: {{ux|en|He's past '''hoping''' for any improvement.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To place [[confidence]]; to [[trust]] with confident expectation of good {{+obj|en|:in}}.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Psalms|cxix|81|text=I '''hope''' in thy word.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Psalms|xlii|11|text=Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? '''Hope''' thou in God.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|dialectal|nonstandard}} To [[wish]].
#: {{ux|en|I '''hope''' you all the best.}}

